        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T16:36:40.089Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Spot Instances offer significant savings, while Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) can reclaim them with a 2-minute warning when capacity is needed elsewhere.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/cost-optimizing-assemblyai-speech-to-text-inference-on-aws-with-amazon-ec2-spot/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T19:35:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T16:36:40.089Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The architecture uses Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS), Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) Spot Instances, and Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/cost-optimizing-assemblyai-speech-to-text-inference-on-aws-with-amazon-ec2-spot/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T19:35:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T16:36:40.089Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The fleet mixes Amazon EC2 Spot Instances and On-Demand Instances across multiple NVIDIA GPU instance families, running a single inference model per GPU at a scale of thousands of instances.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/cost-optimizing-assemblyai-speech-to-text-inference-on-aws-with-amazon-ec2-spot/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T19:35:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T16:36:40.089Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Figure 1: AssemblyAI’s inference architecture on Amazon ECS with Amazon EC2 Spot GPU instances and an Amazon SQS-based retry mechanism",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/cost-optimizing-assemblyai-speech-to-text-inference-on-aws-with-amazon-ec2-spot/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T19:35:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T16:36:40.089Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The cluster hosts GPU-backed ECS tasks (shown as ECS Task, GPU Spot 1 and ECS Task GPU Spot 2) that poll the queue and process inference jobs.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/cost-optimizing-assemblyai-speech-to-text-inference-on-aws-with-amazon-ec2-spot/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T19:35:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T16:36:40.089Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Each task retrieves audio files from Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) and writes the completed transcription to a results store, which AssemblyAI configures to deliver the output to the end customer.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/cost-optimizing-assemblyai-speech-to-text-inference-on-aws-with-amazon-ec2-spot/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T19:35:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T16:36:40.089Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Rather than depending on a single GPU instance family, AssemblyAI’s infrastructure spans three Amazon EC2 GPU instance families:",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/cost-optimizing-assemblyai-speech-to-text-inference-on-aws-with-amazon-ec2-spot/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T19:35:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T16:36:40.089Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Using the price-capacity optimized allocation strategy , Amazon EC2 provisions instances from the Spot capacity pools with the highest available capacity at the lowest price, reducing the likelihood of interruptions.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/cost-optimizing-assemblyai-speech-to-text-inference-on-aws-with-amazon-ec2-spot/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T19:35:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T16:36:40.089Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "By running Amazon EC2 Spot Instances with GPUs in production, AssemblyAI achieved 70 percent cost savings on inference compute compared to On-Demand pricing.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/cost-optimizing-assemblyai-speech-to-text-inference-on-aws-with-amazon-ec2-spot/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T19:35:35.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T16:36:40.089Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "To evaluate Spot availability for your workload, explore using Spot placement scores for accelerated compute and Amazon EC2 Spot Instances best practices .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/cost-optimizing-assemblyai-speech-to-text-inference-on-aws-with-amazon-ec2-spot/",
